Townsaver - Only works to protect innocents...probably pretty useless
            for Nethack (you have to protecting someone who is unarmed...
            and I doubt your pet would count)
Shieldbreaker - Works really well against opponnents that are wielding
                weapons, but useless against those that aren't.
Farslayer - Can be 'thrown' to kill an opponent that is anywhere, but
            does not return
Dragonslicer - hmm..bet you can guess on this one
Stonecutter - Cuts through stone
Wayfinder - Finds path towards what a person wants most
Coinspinner - Increases luck

I don't remember what the names of the other Swords are, and I can't
find my copy of the First Book of Swords, or I'd grace this note
with the poem that describes them all.  There's also one that deals
with healing, deception, and I think mind control (Mindbender?).  Each
of the swords also has a more 'formal' name, such as the Sword of Vengeance
for Farslayer.  Also, some really wierd things happen if you hold two
of them at the same time.

It was actually a pretty decent series, but I think the original 3
Books of Swords are out of print.  There's also a followup series called
The Xth Book of Lost Swords (with X being a number from one to 12).  The 
author is Fred Saberhagen.

